.el .ds Aq '
.TH crisk-render 1  "render 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
crisk\-render \- Render an assessment (or a Statement) in another format, after validating it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcrisk render\fR [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Render an assessment (or a Statement) in another format, after validating it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR
Output format; inferred from the \-\-output name when omitted, else `table`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json: The assessment, as RFC 8785 JSON
.IP \(bu 2
table: A summary for people
.IP \(bu 2
markdown: A summary in Markdown, for a job summary or a merge request note
.IP \(bu 2
in\-toto: An unsigned in\-toto Statement v1 whose subject is the head commit
.IP \(bu 2
sarif: SARIF 2.1.0, one result per reason that names paths
.IP \(bu 2
codequality: GitLab Code Quality, one issue per reason and path
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fI<TIER>\fR
Exit 1 when the tier is at or above TIER (emergency is above high)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
low
.IP \(bu 2
standard
.IP \(bu 2
high
.IP \(bu 2
emergency
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
An assessment, or an in\-toto Statement whose predicate is one
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
